      "tests": [
        {
          "id": "photmad_jvalues_lev1",
          "description": "Reference: the WRF-Chem 4.8 em_scm_xy single-column run (chem_opt = 101 RADM2 KPP, phot_opt = 1 Madronich), 37.6 N 96.7 W, 1999-10-22 19:00 UTC start, dt = 60 s; GNU gfortran 13.3 REAL*4 build; run directory data/eqwefic/chem_scm_phot; dumped by the ctessum-claude/WRF fork, branch earthsciml-instrumented-chem, inside photolysis_mad at call 1410, radiative-transfer level 1. The column is completely CLEAR at this call, so the RT grid is the plain 70-interface extended grid and trapez's interpolation back onto the model levels is the identity for levels 1..60 -- which is why the expected values below are taken straight from phot1_s. The three actinic-flux components are supplied from the dump: this stage verifies the j-value ASSEMBLY (cross section times quantum yield integrated over the 101 active bins), not the two-stream solve that produces the fluxes. Expected values are phot1_s, which is bit-for-bit jv(1:21) of the RADM2 integrator (verified to 1.1e-7 relative across four calls). Single-precision reference, rel 1e-5.",
